IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ohs-dates`
IMPORT `ohs-core`

-- Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004 (Vic) -- from the seat of the person at work.
--
-- SEAT: the individual the Act protects at work: an employee (including a labour hire worker, s 5A, and an independent
-- contractor or a contractor's employee, s 21(3)), or a visitor or member of the public exposed to a business's risks
-- (s 23), and, after a death at work, the family member asking about it. "What does my employer owe me? Has it breached
-- that? What must I do myself? Must I be consulted? Must the incident be reported, and can I see the record? Can unsafe
-- work be stopped, and am I paid meanwhile? What can I do if I was punished for raising safety, and by when? Can I make
-- WorkSafe prosecute? Was the death workplace manslaughter? What is the most the business or its officers can be made to
-- pay?" Every question is asked as that person would ask it, on facts they can state; the court's and the inspector's
-- judgments are facts the person answers from what they have been told. The rules are in ohs-core.l4; this module
-- builds their inputs from plain answers and restates no rule. Inputs with the same meaning have the same name in every
-- question, so the form can ask them once.
--
-- MAYBE BOOLEAN answers: JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE the text says no on these facts; NOTHING the text does not settle it.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004 -- the questions of the person at work`

§§ `What my employer owes me (ss 5, 5A, 20, 21, 23, 34, 152)`

@export Does the business I work for owe me the general duty of s 21 of Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004 to provide and maintain a working environment that is safe and without risks to health?
GIVEN `I am employed under a contract of employment or training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the business's employee under a contract of employment or a contract of training (apprenticeship or traineeship)
      `a labour hire provider supplied, recruited or placed me with the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a labour hire provider supplied you to the business, recruited you for it or placed you with it to work for it
      `the regulations exclude the business or me from the labour hire rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations exclude the business, or you, from being treated as employer and employee under s 5A (if you do not know, answer no)
      `I am an independent contractor the business engaged, or a contractor's employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business engaged you as an independent contractor, or you work for an independent contractor it engaged
      `the matter is within the business's control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk concerns a matter the business controls, or would control but for an agreement limiting its control
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my employer owe me the s 21 duty` IS
    `the s 21 duty is owed (s 21(3))`
        (`is an employee of the employer (ss 5, 5A)` `I am employed under a contract of employment or training` `a labour hire provider supplied, recruited or placed me with the business` `the regulations exclude the business or me from the labour hire rule`)
        `I am an independent contractor the business engaged, or a contractor's employee`
        `the matter is within the business's control`

@export Has the business I work for breached its s 21 duty to keep my working environment safe, on the facts and the findings I give?
GIVEN `I am employed under a contract of employment or training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the business's employee under a contract of employment or a contract of training (apprenticeship or traineeship)
      `a labour hire provider supplied, recruited or placed me with the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a labour hire provider supplied you to the business, recruited you for it or placed you with it to work for it
      `the regulations exclude the business or me from the labour hire rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations exclude the business, or you, from being treated as employer and employee under s 5A (if you do not know, answer no)
      `I am an independent contractor the business engaged, or a contractor's employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business engaged you as an independent contractor, or you work for an independent contractor it engaged
      `the matter is within the business's control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk concerns a matter the business controls, or would control but for an agreement limiting its control
      `the business complied with regulations or a compliance code for this duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business complied with regulations or a WorkSafe compliance code that deal with this duty (s 152 then treats it as having complied)
      `it failed to provide safe plant or systems of work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it failed, so far as reasonably practicable, to provide or maintain plant or systems of work that are safe and without risks to health (s 21(2)(a))
      `it failed to make safe arrangements for plant or substances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it failed to make arrangements for safety in using, handling, storing or transporting plant or substances (s 21(2)(b))
      `it failed to keep the workplace safe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it failed, so far as reasonably practicable, to keep a workplace it manages and controls safe and without risks to health (s 21(2)(c))
      `it failed to provide adequate welfare facilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it failed, so far as reasonably practicable, to provide adequate welfare facilities such as toilets, drinking water, meal areas and first aid (s 21(2)(d))
      `it failed to give necessary information, instruction, training or supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it failed to give the information, instruction, training or supervision needed for you to work safely (s 21(2)(e))
      `the risk was eliminated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk to health or safety was eliminated
      `eliminating the risk was reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was reasonably practicable to eliminate the risk, weighing likelihood, harm, knowledge, available means and cost (s 20(2)); a question for the court
      `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable (s 20(1)(b)); a question for the court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer breached its s 21 duty to me` IS
    `the employer contravened s 21(1)`
        (`Does my employer owe me the s 21 duty` `I am employed under a contract of employment or training` `a labour hire provider supplied, recruited or placed me with the business` `the regulations exclude the business or me from the labour hire rule` `I am an independent contractor the business engaged, or a contractor's employee` `the matter is within the business's control`)
        `the business complied with regulations or a compliance code for this duty`
        `it failed to provide safe plant or systems of work`
        `it failed to make safe arrangements for plant or substances`
        `it failed to keep the workplace safe`
        `it failed to provide adequate welfare facilities`
        `it failed to give necessary information, instruction, training or supervision`
        (`the s 20 standard is met` `the risk was eliminated` `eliminating the risk was reasonably practicable` `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable`)

@export I am not the business's employee (a visitor, customer, member of the public, or someone else's worker): has it breached its s 23 duty not to expose me to risks from the way it runs its business?
GIVEN `I am employed under a contract of employment or training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the business's employee under a contract of employment or a contract of training (apprenticeship or traineeship)
      `a labour hire provider supplied, recruited or placed me with the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a labour hire provider supplied you to the business, recruited you for it or placed you with it to work for it
      `the regulations exclude the business or me from the labour hire rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations exclude the business, or you, from being treated as employer and employee under s 5A (if you do not know, answer no)
      `the risk arose from the conduct of the business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk you were exposed to arose from the way the business conducts its undertaking
      `the business complied with regulations or a compliance code for this duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business complied with regulations or a WorkSafe compliance code that deal with this duty (s 152 then treats it as having complied)
      `the risk was eliminated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk to health or safety was eliminated
      `eliminating the risk was reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was reasonably practicable to eliminate the risk, weighing likelihood, harm, knowledge, available means and cost (s 20(2)); a question for the court
      `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable (s 20(1)(b)); a question for the court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the business breached its s 23 duty to me` IS
    `the employer contravened s 23(1)`
        (`is an employee of the employer (ss 5, 5A)` `I am employed under a contract of employment or training` `a labour hire provider supplied, recruited or placed me with the business` `the regulations exclude the business or me from the labour hire rule`)
        `the risk arose from the conduct of the business`
        `the business complied with regulations or a compliance code for this duty`
        (`the s 20 standard is met` `the risk was eliminated` `eliminating the risk was reasonably practicable` `the risk was reduced so far as reasonably practicable`)

@export Does Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004 itself give me a right to sue for compensation because a duty in Part 3 (the general duties) was breached? (No: s 34 says Part 3 creates no civil right of action and takes none away; claims are made under the workers' compensation and common law.)
GIVEN `the provision breached` IS AN `Offence` @desc The provision you say was breached
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this Act give me a right to sue for the breach` IS
    IF `is a Part 3 offence` `the provision breached`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `My own duties at work (ss 25, 32)`

@export Have I breached my own duties as an employee under s 25 of Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004 (reasonable care for myself and others, co-operating with my employer, not misusing safety equipment)?
GIVEN `I was at work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this happened while you were at work
      `I failed to take reasonable care for my own health and safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to take reasonable care for your own health and safety, judged on what you knew at the time (s 25(3))
      `I failed to take reasonable care for others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to take reasonable care for people your acts or omissions at the workplace may affect, judged on what you knew (s 25(3))
      `I failed to co-operate with my employer's safety measures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you failed to co-operate with something your employer did to comply with the Act or the regulations
      `I intentionally or recklessly interfered with or misused safety equipment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you intentionally or recklessly interfered with or misused anything provided at the workplace for health, safety or welfare
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I breached my duties as an employee` IS
    `the employee contravened s 25` `I was at work` `I failed to take reasonable care for my own health and safety` `I failed to take reasonable care for others` `I failed to co-operate with my employer's safety measures` `I intentionally or recklessly interfered with or misused safety equipment`

@export Is the offence of recklessly endangering a person at a workplace (s 32: up to 5 years' prison or 1800 penalty units for a natural person, 20 000 for a company) made out on these facts?
GIVEN `there was a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person had a lawful excuse for the conduct
      `the conduct was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person engaged in the conduct recklessly (aware of the likely danger and going ahead); a question for the court
      `someone at a workplace was or may have been put in danger of serious injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct placed, or may have placed, another person at a workplace in danger of serious injury
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is reckless endangerment made out` IS
    `the s 32 offence is made out` `there was a lawful excuse` `the conduct was reckless` `someone at a workplace was or may have been put in danger of serious injury`

§§ `Being consulted (s 35)`

@export Must my employer consult me about this health and safety matter under s 35 of Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Consultation matter` @desc What the employer is doing: identifying or assessing hazards; deciding control measures; deciding welfare facilities; deciding procedures (issue resolution, consultation, monitoring, information and training); deciding health and safety committee membership; proposing changes to the workplace, plant, substances or work; something the regulations prescribe; or something else
      `I am or am likely to be directly affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, or are likely to be, directly affected by what the employer is doing
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer consult me` IS
    `the employer must consult the employee (s 35(1))` `the matter` `I am or am likely to be directly affected`

@export Must my employer's consultation with me involve my health and safety representative (s 35(4))?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Consultation matter` @desc What the employer is doing: identifying or assessing hazards; deciding control measures; deciding welfare facilities; deciding procedures (issue resolution, consultation, monitoring, information and training); deciding health and safety committee membership; proposing changes to the workplace, plant, substances or work; something the regulations prescribe; or something else
      `I am or am likely to be directly affected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are, or are likely to be, directly affected by what the employer is doing
      `I am represented by a health and safety representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in a designated work group that has an elected health and safety representative
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the consultation involve my representative` IS
    CONSIDER `the employer must consult the employee (s 35(1))` `the matter` `I am or am likely to be directly affected`
    WHEN JUST `must consult` THEN
        IF `must consult`
        THEN IF `I am represented by a health and safety representative` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `After an incident at work (ss 37-39) -- only if there has been an incident`

@export Must WorkSafe be notified of this incident at work under ss 37 and 38 of Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004?
GIVEN `what the incident caused` IS AN `Incident outcome` @desc What the incident caused, or the serious risk it exposed someone to: a death; medical treatment within 48 hours of exposure to a substance; immediate in-patient treatment; immediate medical treatment for a listed serious injury; a serious risk from an immediate or imminent exposure to one of the listed dangers; something the regulations prescribe; or none of these
      `the regulations exclude this kind of incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations exclude this kind of incident (if you do not know, answer no)
      `it happened at a workplace the business manages and controls` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the incident happened at a workplace under the management and control of the employer or self-employed person
      `the business is aware of the incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer or self-employed person has become aware that the incident happened
      `the only person harmed or exposed was the self-employed person themself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only person injured, harmed or exposed to risk was the employer or self-employed person themself (answer no if anyone else was)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must WorkSafe be notified of the incident` IF
    `the incident must be notified (s 38(1), (2))` (`Part 5 applies to the incident (s 37)` `what the incident caused` `the regulations exclude this kind of incident`) `it happened at a workplace the business manages and controls` `the business is aware of the incident` `the only person harmed or exposed was the self-employed person themself`

@export Was, or is, the written record of the incident given to WorkSafe in time (within 48 hours after the duty to notify arose, s 38(3))? Yes, no, or not yet known while the 48 hours are still running.
GIVEN `what the incident caused` IS AN `Incident outcome` @desc What the incident caused, or the serious risk it exposed someone to: a death; medical treatment within 48 hours of exposure to a substance; immediate in-patient treatment; immediate medical treatment for a listed serious injury; a serious risk from an immediate or imminent exposure to one of the listed dangers; something the regulations prescribe; or none of these
      `the regulations exclude this kind of incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations exclude this kind of incident (if you do not know, answer no)
      `it happened at a workplace the business manages and controls` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the incident happened at a workplace under the management and control of the employer or self-employed person
      `the business is aware of the incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer or self-employed person has become aware that the incident happened
      `the only person harmed or exposed was the self-employed person themself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only person injured, harmed or exposed to risk was the employer or self-employed person themself (answer no if anyone else was)
      `the record has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business has given WorkSafe a written record of the incident
      `hours from becoming aware to the record` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours after the business became aware of the incident it gave WorkSafe the written record (0 if not yet given)
      `hours since becoming aware` IS A NUMBER @desc How many hours have passed since the business became aware of the incident
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was the incident record given in time` IS
    IF NOT `Must WorkSafe be notified of the incident` `what the incident caused` `the regulations exclude this kind of incident` `it happened at a workplace the business manages and controls` `the business is aware of the incident` `the only person harmed or exposed was the self-employed person themself`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the record has been given`
         THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 38(3) -- the written record of the incident within 48 hours` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the duty-holder` `give the Authority a written record of the incident` `hours from becoming aware to the record`))
              WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST TRUE
              OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `hours since becoming aware` GREATER THAN 48
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE NOTHING

@export Must the business let me see its written record of the incident (s 38(4))?
GIVEN `who I am` IS A `Record inspector` @desc Who you are: a person injured in the incident or exposed to serious risk by it; their representative; the representative of a person the incident killed; the health and safety representative for your designated work group; a member of the employer's health and safety committee; or someone else
      `the business is an employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business that must keep the record is an employer (answer no for a self-employed person with no employees)
      `the record was given to WorkSafe on` IS A DATE @desc The day the business gave WorkSafe the written record of the incident
      `the day I ask` IS A DATE @desc The day you ask to see the record
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I see the incident record` IS
    `the record must be made available (s 38(4))` `who I am` `the business is an employer` `the record was given to WorkSafe on` `the day I ask`

@export May the site of the incident be disturbed now (s 39), or must it be left as it is until a WorkSafe inspector arrives?
GIVEN `what the incident caused` IS AN `Incident outcome` @desc What the incident caused, or the serious risk it exposed someone to: a death; medical treatment within 48 hours of exposure to a substance; immediate in-patient treatment; immediate medical treatment for a listed serious injury; a serious risk from an immediate or imminent exposure to one of the listed dangers; something the regulations prescribe; or none of these
      `the regulations exclude this kind of incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations exclude this kind of incident (if you do not know, answer no)
      `it happened at a workplace the business manages and controls` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the incident happened at a workplace under the management and control of the employer or self-employed person
      `the business is aware of the incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer or self-employed person has become aware that the incident happened
      `the only person harmed or exposed was the self-employed person themself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the only person injured, harmed or exposed to risk was the employer or self-employed person themself (answer no if anyone else was)
      `an inspector has arrived at the site` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a WorkSafe inspector has arrived at the site
      `the time an inspector directed has come` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an inspector, when WorkSafe was notified, directed that the site may be disturbed from some time, and that time has come
      `it is to protect someone, help an injured person, or make the site safe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the site would be disturbed to protect someone's health or safety, to help an injured person, or for essential action to make the site safe or prevent another incident
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the incident site be disturbed` IS
    `the site may be disturbed (s 39)`
        (`Must WorkSafe be notified of the incident` `what the incident caused` `the regulations exclude this kind of incident` `it happened at a workplace the business manages and controls` `the business is aware of the incident` `the only person harmed or exposed was the self-employed person themself`)
        `an inspector has arrived at the site`
        `the time an inspector directed has come`
        `it is to protect someone, help an injured person, or make the site safe`

§§ `Unsafe work (ss 73-75) -- only if a health or safety issue has arisen`

@export Can the unsafe work be stopped by a direction to cease work under s 74 of Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004?
GIVEN `a health or safety issue has arisen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an issue about health or safety has arisen at the workplace or from the way the employer runs its business
      `the work involves an immediate threat to health or safety` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the issue concerns work that involves an immediate threat to anyone's health or safety
      `it is not appropriate to use the usual issue resolution procedure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, given the threat and the degree of risk, it is not appropriate to follow the usual issue resolution procedure (s 73)
      `the employer and the representative have consulted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer and the health and safety representative have consulted each other about it
      `who would direct` IS A `Who directs` @desc Who would give the direction: the employer; the health and safety representative for the designated work group; or someone else (for example an employee who is not the representative)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the work be stopped` IS
    `work may be directed to cease (s 74)` `a health or safety issue has arisen` `the work involves an immediate threat to health or safety` `it is not appropriate to use the usual issue resolution procedure` `the employer and the representative have consulted` `who would direct`

@export Can I ask WorkSafe to send an inspector to my workplace about a health or safety issue (s 75(1))?
GIVEN `I am a party trying to resolve the issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are one of the parties trying to resolve the issue: an employee affected by it, their health and safety representative, or the employer
      `it has not been resolved within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the issue has not been resolved under the issue resolution procedure within a reasonable time
      `work was directed to cease` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the issue is the subject of a direction under s 74 that work cease
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I ask for an inspector` IS
    `an inspector may be requested (s 75(1))` `I am a party trying to resolve the issue` `it has not been resolved within a reasonable time` `work was directed to cease`

@export Am I still entitled to be paid for the time I did not work because of a health or safety issue (s 75(4))?
GIVEN `I did not work because of the issue while it was unresolved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as a result of the issue arising, you did not work for a period while it was being resolved
      `I would otherwise have been entitled to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would otherwise have been entitled to be paid for that period
      `the inspector issued a prohibition notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the inspector who attended issued a prohibition notice
      `the inspector decided in writing there was reasonable cause for concern` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the inspector decided, in writing, that there was reasonable cause for employees to be concerned for their health or safety
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I still paid for the time I did not work` IS
    `pay continues (s 75(4))` `I did not work because of the issue while it was unresolved` `I would otherwise have been entitled to be paid` `the inspector issued a prohibition notice` `the inspector decided in writing there was reasonable cause for concern`

§§ `If I was punished for raising health and safety (ss 76-78E) -- only if this has happened`

@export Has my employer (or a prospective employer) discriminated against me for a health and safety reason in breach of s 78A, so that I can bring a civil claim in the Industrial Division of the Magistrates' Court?
GIVEN `what was done to me` IS A `Treatment` @desc What the employer did: dismissed you; injured you in your employment; altered your position to your detriment; threatened one of those; refused or failed to offer you a job; treated you less favourably than another applicant in the terms offered; or none of these
      `why it was done` IS A `Reason` @desc The reason you say it was done: being or having been a health and safety representative or committee member; exercising a power as one; assisting or giving information to an inspector, WorkSafe, a union authorised representative, a representative or committee member; raising a health or safety issue or concern; or another reason
      `that reason was a substantial reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that reason was a substantial reason for what was done (s 78B(2)); the employer must prove it was not, once the other facts are proved (s 78E(2))
      `the conduct was reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer proves that what it did was reasonable in the circumstances (s 78E(3)(a))
      `a substantial reason was to comply with safety or workers' compensation law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer proves that a substantial reason was to comply with this Act or the Workplace Injury Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2013 (s 78E(3)(b))
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has my employer discriminated against me under s 78A` IS
    `s 78A is contravened` `what was done to me` `why it was done` `that reason was a substantial reason` `the conduct was reasonable in the circumstances` `a substantial reason was to comply with safety or workers' compensation law`

@export Could my employer be guilty of the criminal offence in s 76 for discriminating against me for a health and safety reason (up to 500 penalty units for a natural person, 2500 for a company)?
GIVEN `what was done to me` IS A `Treatment` @desc What the employer did: dismissed you; injured you in your employment; altered your position to your detriment; threatened one of those; refused or failed to offer you a job; treated you less favourably than another applicant in the terms offered; or none of these
      `why it was done` IS A `Reason` @desc The reason you say it was done: being or having been a health and safety representative or committee member; exercising a power as one; assisting or giving information to an inspector, WorkSafe, a union authorised representative, a representative or committee member; raising a health or safety issue or concern; or another reason
      `that reason was the dominant reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that reason was the dominant reason for what was done (s 76(3)); the employer must prove it was not, once the other facts are proved (s 77)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Could my employer be guilty under s 76` IS
    `the s 76 offence is made out` `what was done to me` `why it was done` `that reason was the dominant reason`

@export By when must I start my civil proceeding for discrimination under ss 78A and 78D (s 78E(1): not more than 1 year after I knew or ought to have known the cause of action accrued)?
GIVEN `the day I knew or ought to have known of my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you knew, or ought to have known, that you had a cause of action (usually the day of the dismissal or other treatment, or when you learned why it was done)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I start my discrimination claim` IS
    `the last day to commence a s 78D proceeding (s 78E(1))` `the day I knew or ought to have known of my claim`

@export Is my civil proceeding for discrimination under ss 78A and 78D started in time, if I start it on the day I give?
GIVEN `the day I knew or ought to have known of my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you knew, or ought to have known, that you had a cause of action (usually the day of the dismissal or other treatment, or when you learned why it was done)
      `the day I start the proceeding` IS A DATE @desc The day the proceeding is, or will be, filed in the Industrial Division of the Magistrates' Court
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my discrimination claim in time` IF
    `the day I start the proceeding` `is no later than` (`By when must I start my discrimination claim` `the day I knew or ought to have known of my claim`)

@export Can the Industrial Division of the Magistrates' Court order compensation, reinstatement or other remedies for me under s 78D?
GIVEN `I am affected by the contravention, or authorised to represent someone who is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a person affected by the discriminatory conduct, or someone authorised to represent that person (s 78D(5))
      `the employer contravened s 78A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employer engaged in discriminatory conduct for a prohibited reason (the court's finding, or your answer from the s 78A question)
      `a criminal court already ordered damages or reinstatement under s 78 for the same conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after convicting the employer under s 76 for the same conduct, a court has already made an order for damages or reinstatement under s 78
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the court make a s 78D order for me` IS
    IF NOT `I am affected by the contravention, or authorised to represent someone who is`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a criminal court already ordered damages or reinstatement under s 78 for the same conduct`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the employer contravened s 78A` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE

@export Once everything except the employer's reason is proved, must my employer prove that the health and safety reason was not its reason (ss 77, 78E(2))?
GIVEN `everything except the reason is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all the facts of the discriminatory conduct other than the reason for it have been proved
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer prove its reason` IS
    IF `everything except the reason is proved` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Making WorkSafe prosecute (ss 131, 132) -- only if I think an offence was committed`

@export May I ask WorkSafe in writing to bring a prosecution for what happened (s 131(1): only once 6 months have passed without a prosecution)?
GIVEN `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day of the act or event you consider to be an offence
      `a prosecution was brought within 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a prosecution has been brought for it within 6 months of that day
      `the day I ask` IS A DATE @desc The day you would make the written request
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask WorkSafe to prosecute` IS
    IF `a prosecution was brought within 6 months`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF (`the first day a s 131 request may be made` `the day it happened`) `is no later than` `the day I ask`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

@export By when must WorkSafe answer my written request to prosecute (s 131(2), (2A): within 3 months after receiving it)?
GIVEN `the day WorkSafe received my request` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe received your written request
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must WorkSafe answer my request` IS
    `the Authority's reply is due by (s 131(2), (2A))` `the day WorkSafe received my request`

@export Has WorkSafe answered my request to prosecute in time? Yes, no, or not yet known while the 3 months are still running.
GIVEN `the day WorkSafe received my request` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe received your written request
      `WorkSafe has answered in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe has given you its written advice or report
      `the day WorkSafe answered` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe gave you its written advice or report (any day if it has not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has WorkSafe answered in time` IS
    IF `WorkSafe has answered in writing`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 131(2) -- the Authority must report to the person who asked within 3 months` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Authority` `report in writing to the person who made the request` (`the days from` `the day WorkSafe received my request` `to` `the day WorkSafe answered`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `today` `is after` (`By when must WorkSafe answer my request` `the day WorkSafe received my request`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the days allowed` MEANS `the days from` `the day WorkSafe received my request` `to` (`By when must WorkSafe answer my request` `the day WorkSafe received my request`)

@export May I ask WorkSafe to refer my request to the Director of Public Prosecutions (s 131(3))?
GIVEN `the day WorkSafe received my request` IS A DATE @desc The day WorkSafe received your written request
      `WorkSafe advised it will not prosecute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe has advised you that a prosecution will not be brought
      `WorkSafe has brought a prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether WorkSafe has brought a prosecution
      `the day I ask` IS A DATE @desc The day you would make the written request
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask for a referral to the DPP` IS
    IF     `WorkSafe advised it will not prosecute`
        OR ((NOT `WorkSafe has brought a prosecution`) AND (`the day I ask` `is after` (`the day` 9 `months after` `the day WorkSafe received my request`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@export Can the offence still be prosecuted under the time limits in s 132 of Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence: the provision said to be contravened
      `it is an officer's offence for the company's workplace manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charge is against an officer under s 144(1) for a body corporate's workplace manslaughter (s 39G(1))
      `the day it came to WorkSafe's notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence first came to WorkSafe's notice
      `a coroner's report or inquest showed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a coronial report, inquiry or inquest made it appear that an indictable offence against the Act had been committed
      `the day the coroner reported or the inquest ended` IS A DATE @desc The day the coronial report was made or the inquiry or inquest ended (any day if there was none)
      `a WorkSafe undertaking was contravened or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a s 16 enforceable undertaking was given for the offence and was then contravened, its contravention came to WorkSafe's notice, or WorkSafe agreed to its withdrawal
      `the day of that undertaking event` IS A DATE @desc The day of that contravention, notice or withdrawal (any day if there was none)
      `the DPP authorised the prosecution in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Director of Public Prosecutions has authorised the prosecution in writing
      `the court accepts fresh evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether fresh evidence was found and the court is satisfied it could not reasonably have been found within the limitation period (s 132(2))
      `the day of the prosecution` IS A DATE @desc The day the prosecution is, or would be, brought
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can it still be prosecuted` IS
    IF `is a workplace manslaughter offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF NOT `is an indictable offence` `the offence`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF     `the DPP authorised the prosecution in writing`
                  OR `the court accepts fresh evidence`
                  OR `the day of the prosecution` `is no later than` (`the last day of the s 132(1) limitation period` `the day it came to WorkSafe's notice` `a coroner's report or inquest showed an offence` `the day the coroner reported or the inquest ended` `a WorkSafe undertaking was contravened or withdrawn` `the day of that undertaking event`)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `is a workplace manslaughter offence` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the offence`
            WHEN `s 39G(1) workplace manslaughter` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `s 39G(2) workplace manslaughter by an officer` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE `it is an officer's offence for the company's workplace manslaughter`

@export What is the last day for prosecuting the offence under s 132(1), unless the DPP authorises a later prosecution or fresh evidence is found? (None for workplace manslaughter, which may be prosecuted at any time; not settled here for a summary offence.)
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence: the provision said to be contravened
      `it is an officer's offence for the company's workplace manslaughter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charge is against an officer under s 144(1) for a body corporate's workplace manslaughter (s 39G(1))
      `the day it came to WorkSafe's notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence first came to WorkSafe's notice
      `a coroner's report or inquest showed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a coronial report, inquiry or inquest made it appear that an indictable offence against the Act had been committed
      `the day the coroner reported or the inquest ended` IS A DATE @desc The day the coronial report was made or the inquiry or inquest ended (any day if there was none)
      `a WorkSafe undertaking was contravened or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a s 16 enforceable undertaking was given for the offence and was then contravened, its contravention came to WorkSafe's notice, or WorkSafe agreed to its withdrawal
      `the day of that undertaking event` IS A DATE @desc The day of that contravention, notice or withdrawal (any day if there was none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `What is the last day to prosecute` IS
    IF `is a manslaughter charge`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF NOT `is an indictable offence` `the offence`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST (`the last day of the s 132(1) limitation period` `the day it came to WorkSafe's notice` `a coroner's report or inquest showed an offence` `the day the coroner reported or the inquest ended` `a WorkSafe undertaking was contravened or withdrawn` `the day of that undertaking event`)
    WHERE
        `is a manslaughter charge` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the offence`
            WHEN `s 39G(1) workplace manslaughter` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `s 39G(2) workplace manslaughter by an officer` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE `it is an officer's offence for the company's workplace manslaughter`

§§ `A death at work: workplace manslaughter (Part 5A) -- only if someone died`

@export Was the death workplace manslaughter by the employer or other duty-holder (s 39G(1) of Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004: up to 25 years' prison for a natural person, 100 000 penalty units for a company)?
GIVEN `the duty` IS A `Part 3 duty` @desc The Part 3 duty said to be breached (for an employer, usually s 21 for a worker or s 23 for anyone else)
      `the duty-holder was an employee and not an officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who owed the duty was an employee, and not an officer, at the workplace (this matters only for s 32)
      `the person who died belonged to the class the duty protects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was someone the duty is owed to, or whose health and safety it is meant to protect (for s 21 a worker; for s 23 someone who was not an employee)
      `the conduct began on` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct (an act, or a failure to act) began
      `the duty-holder was a volunteer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person said to be guilty was acting as a volunteer
      `the conduct was a great falling short of the standard of care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct fell greatly short of the care a reasonable person (or reasonable company) would have taken; a question for the court
      `the conduct involved a high risk of death, serious injury or serious illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct involved a high risk of death, serious injury or serious illness; a question for the court
      `the conduct breached the duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct was a breach of that duty (other conduct may have contributed too, s 39D)
      `the conduct caused the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct caused the death; a question for the court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was it workplace manslaughter` IS
    `s 39G is contravened`
        `the conduct began on`
        `the duty-holder was a volunteer`
        (`the conduct is negligent (s 39E)` `the conduct was a great falling short of the standard of care` `the conduct involved a high risk of death, serious injury or serious illness`)
        `the conduct breached the duty`
        (`owes an applicable duty to the deceased (s 39F)` `the duty` `the duty-holder was an employee and not an officer` `the person who died belonged to the class the duty protects`)
        `the conduct caused the death`

@export Was the death workplace manslaughter by an officer (a director or senior decision-maker) of the company, partnership or association whose duty was breached (s 39G(2): up to 25 years' prison)?
GIVEN `the duty` IS A `Part 3 duty` @desc The Part 3 duty of the company, partnership or association said to be breached (for an employer, usually s 21 for a worker or s 23 for anyone else)
      `the person who died belonged to the class the duty protects` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who died was someone the duty is owed to, or whose health and safety it is meant to protect (for s 21 a worker; for s 23 someone who was not an employee)
      `the entity is a company, partnership or association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body whose duty was breached is a body corporate, an unincorporated body or association, or a partnership (whether or not it represents the Crown)
      `the person is an officer of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person said to be guilty is an officer of that body (a director, secretary, or someone who makes or takes part in decisions affecting the whole or a substantial part of its business)
      `the conduct began on` IS A DATE @desc The day the conduct (an act, or a failure to act) began
      `the duty-holder was a volunteer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person said to be guilty was acting as a volunteer
      `the conduct was a great falling short of the standard of care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct fell greatly short of the care a reasonable person (or reasonable company) would have taken; a question for the court
      `the conduct involved a high risk of death, serious injury or serious illness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct involved a high risk of death, serious injury or serious illness; a question for the court
      `the conduct breached the duty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct was a breach of that duty (other conduct may have contributed too, s 39D)
      `the conduct caused the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the conduct caused the death; a question for the court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- The entity's duty: s 39B(b) excludes s 32 only for a duty-holder who is an employee and not an officer, so FALSE.
DECIDE `Was it workplace manslaughter by an officer` IS
    IF NOT (`the entity is a company, partnership or association` AND `the person is an officer of it`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `s 39G is contravened`
            `the conduct began on`
            `the duty-holder was a volunteer`
            (`the conduct is negligent (s 39E)` `the conduct was a great falling short of the standard of care` `the conduct involved a high risk of death, serious injury or serious illness`)
            `the conduct breached the duty`
            (`owes an applicable duty to the deceased (s 39F)` `the duty` FALSE `the person who died belonged to the class the duty protects`)
            `the conduct caused the death`

§§ `What can be imposed (ss 21-39G, 76, 139, 144, 145, 148A, 148B, 153)`

@export What is the most a court can fine for this offence under Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004, in penalty units (0 where the Act sets imprisonment only)?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence: the provision said to be contravened
      `the offender` IS AN `Offender` @desc Whether the offender is a natural person (an individual) or a body corporate (a company)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most the court can fine` IS
    `the maximum fine in penalty units` `the offence` `the offender`

@export What is the longest prison term for this offence under Victoria's Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004, in years (0 where the Act sets a fine only)?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence: the provision said to be contravened
      `the offender` IS AN `Offender` @desc Whether the offender is a natural person (an individual) or a body corporate (a company)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest prison term` IS
    `the maximum imprisonment in years` `the offence` `the offender`

@export Can an officer of the company, partnership or association be personally guilty of its offence under ss 144 and 145?
GIVEN `the entity contravened the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the company (or, for a partnership or association, the body) contravened the provision
      `it was because the officer failed to take reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contravention is attributable to the officer failing to take reasonable care, given what they knew and their power over the decisions; a question for the court
      `the officer was acting as a volunteer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what the officer did or failed to do was done as a volunteer
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can an officer be personally guilty` IS
    `the officer is liable (ss 144, 145)` `the entity contravened the provision` `it was because the officer failed to take reasonable care` `the officer was acting as a volunteer`

@export What is the most an officer can be fined, in penalty units, for the company's, partnership's or association's offence (ss 144(1), 145(3))?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence: the provision said to be contravened
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most an officer can be fined` IS
    `the officer's maximum fine in penalty units (ss 144(1), 145(3))` `the offence`

@export If an infringement notice (an on-the-spot fine) is served instead of a prosecution, what is the most it can charge, in penalty units (s 139(2))?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence: the provision said to be contravened
      `the offender` IS AN `Offender` @desc Whether the offender is a natural person (an individual) or a body corporate (a company)
      `the regulations make it an infringement offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations prescribe the offence as one for which an infringement notice may be served (if you do not know, answer no)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most an infringement notice can charge` IS
    `the most an infringement notice may specify (s 139(2))` `the offence` `the offender` `the regulations make it an infringement offence`

@export Can the business's insurance or an indemnity pay a fine or other pecuniary penalty imposed under this Act (ss 148A, 148B)? (No: such a term is void and offering or taking it is an offence; insurance for compensation claims is not affected.)
GIVEN `it is a penalty under this Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the liability is to pay a pecuniary penalty (a fine) under the Occupational Health and Safety Act 2004 or its regulations, as opposed to damages or compensation
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can insurance pay the penalty` IS
    IF `it is a penalty under this Act or the regulations` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
